+/* Porthole voice bridge (Discord branch, patch 0200): Porthole is ONE audio source. The app mixes everything itself, so Discord's sound is added into this
+ * endpoint's output (after the game's own mix and the background mute, so it is heard while the game is paused, muted for the background, or absent) and
+ * the microphone comes in on this same unit (full duplex), not through a second audio engine that would fight this one for the hardware.
+ * Two lock-free single-producer rings of mono float samples at the endpoint's rate:
+ *   playback: the app writes (porthole_voice_write), the render callback reads and puts the same sample on every output channel;
+ *   capture:  the render callback writes what the microphone delivered, the app reads (porthole_voice_read).
+ * Nothing in here blocks the real-time thread. */
+#define PV_RING 16384u    /* frames, power of two: about 340 ms at 48 kHz */
